{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1016651-reign-of-the-exarchs","id":1016651,"title":"Reign of the Exarchs","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-13T11:07:09-08:00","id":1016651,"title":"Reign of the Exarchs","content":"I'm about to start running a new 2e chronicle using this book.<br /> <br /> I have 3 players (Thyrsus Silver Ladder, Obrimos Adamantine Arrow, and Mastigos Mysterium). All are male.<br /> <br /> Does anyone have any advice for running this? Are there any changes due to 2e that you would recommend?<br /> <br /> PS: I've read Broken Diamond already.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T11:47:27-08:00","id":1016666,"title":"","content":"Uncertain why all the players (characters?) being male is relevant to the question.<br /> <br /> I turned each chapter of Reign of the Exarchs into a full-blown chronicle made up of several stories. Most useful advice I have is &quot;use Cymbeline and the Eyes of Salt in an adventure previous to the one in which they appear.&quot;<br /> <br /> Also &quot;If you're gonna use Remainder, do the same thing.&quot;<br /> <br /> Other than that you're pretty much good to go. It's a solid chronicle, in my opinion. I expanded it to include an Heiromagus, and the PC's are currently fighting against a cult that seems to have &quot;Awakened Again,&quot; such that their magic treats the Awakened Mages in the way that Awakened Magic treats sleepers. The Abyss may very well be abolished (or at least, more effectively bridged) by the end of it. We've been running this game for 2+ IRL years now. Been a lot of fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Storytelling is the art of pretending you totally meant for that to happen just now.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12721-evilsqueegee","name":"EvilSqueegee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12721_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T09:58:09-08:00","id":1017120,"title":"","content":"Something specific. <br /> <br /> How is Gawain able to stay two weeks ahead of his pursuers, now that the Warding rules have changed?<br /> <br /> Wouldn't the Seers just keep trying to penetrate the Ward on The Ring by spamming a Space finding spell and find it in short order?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T11:15:53-08:00","id":1017163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1016651-reign-of-the-exarchs?p=1017120#post1017120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How is Gawain able to stay two weeks ahead of his pursuers, now that the Warding rules have changed?<br /> <br /> Wouldn't the Seers just keep trying to penetrate the Ward on The Ring by spamming a Space finding spell and find it in short order?</div> </div> </div> </div>Aiden and Sean both have Space 3 tied for their highest Arcanum, Gawain has four dots in three Arcana including Space, and finding the Ring by Scrying or using Locate Object from more than a neighborhood away requires the Sympathetic Range Attainment, which in turn costs Mana, requires an appropriate sympathetic tool, and necessitates dropping Potency into overcoming the added Withstand rating.<br /> <br /> The process is undoubtedly now more complex than &quot;Gawain put a Ward on the Ring,&quot; but it's still not a trivial matter for a Gnosis 3 Obrimos and a Gnosis 2 Mastigos to track down a third-degree Adept of Space.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":"Gawain's still Gnosis 4, but without speculating on what the Seers' Praxes would be we have to guess that Aiden would be spending extra Mana to use 12-14-2016, 03:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T11:36:32-08:00","id":1017183,"title":"","content":"In other words, even if they managed to pierce the Wards that Gawain has put up, he can work twice as fast as them in ritual time, and has more dice to drop for increasing spell factors regardless of ritual or instant casting. Sure they can always eventually whittle his defense down, but he can keep putting it up and changing location before they can act on their ability to locate him. Co-Location basically is Portal Arcade or whatever that fancy technique he used for throwing off trackers was and for him probably a Praxes or a Rote.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T12:43:39-08:00","id":1017219,"title":"","content":"It's a shame that you can locate anyone by Fating random numbers as coordinates. I really don't understand how can you hide in this game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T12:51:12-08:00","id":1017228,"title":"","content":"Pocket Dimension?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T13:40:41-08:00","id":1017283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1016651-reign-of-the-exarchs?p=1017219#post1017219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a shame that you can locate anyone by Fating random numbers as coordinates.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not how that works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T14:01:28-08:00","id":1017299,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11887_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11887\" data-vbnamecard=\"11887\">Tessie</a> And cut all your sympathetic ties. The side effect is that you end up in prison slowly becoming shadow of your former self. But even then someone can affect you with Temporal Sympathy.<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> Why not? I even remember it from 1ed which was waay more restrictive on magic usage.<br /> <br /> Edit: I feel that this deserves it's own thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T14:03:15-08:00","id":1017300,"title":"","content":"Well, you could always rip out a soul stone to create a demesne and then astral travel to get a change of scenery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T14:08:34-08:00","id":1017305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1016651-reign-of-the-exarchs?p=1017299#post1017299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But even then someone can affect you with Temporal Sympathy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not without straight-up time-travel they can't.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> Why not? I even remember it from 1ed which was waay more restrictive on magic usage. </div> </div> </div>&quot;This magic makes it so that you just so happen to enter the correct inputs for a device to do the thing you're trying to do&quot; is not &quot;you can locate anyone.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T14:28:25-08:00","id":1017315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1016651-reign-of-the-exarchs?p=1017305#post1017305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not without straight-up time-travel they can't.<br /> &quot;This magic makes it so that you just so happen to enter the correct inputs for a device to do the thing you're trying to do&quot; is not &quot;you can locate anyone.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I think they mean &quot;enter the correct inputs for a device to do the thing you're trying to do&quot; where &quot;the thing you're trying to do&quot; is Locate the Ring. So GPS coordinates which happen to be where the Ring is (or anyone, for that matter). As long as they exist in a location that can be modeled by GPS, of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T14:43:32-08:00","id":1017325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1016651-reign-of-the-exarchs?p=1017315#post1017315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think they mean &amp;quot;enter the correct inputs for a device to do the thing you're trying to do&amp;quot; where &amp;quot;the thing you're trying to do&amp;quot; is Locate the Ring. So GPS coordinates which happen to be where the Ring is (or anyone, for that matter). As long as they exist in a location that can be modeled by GPS, of course.</div> </div> </div> </div>At best it would have to be a multiple step process because the gps program doesn't have a way of tracking the Ring's location.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T14:44:41-08:00","id":1017326,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11887_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11887\" data-vbnamecard=\"11887\">Tessie</a> That's a lovely vision. I like that. But still. Cutting or even veiling your sympathies damages you a lot. - But if you are hiding with master level spell you can expect to be hunted by a master level spell. Corridors of Time will get you before you'll enter your safe spot.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> You do realize that there is a whole chapter about creative thaumaturgy? Rulling let's you do things that can happen and bumping into somene is one of those things. It's what Fate does, you wish something and tadaa.<br /> And well. I hate this little paragraph in Time about using attainmant only with spells that ask for it. It's a throwback to 1ed when you didn't knew the principles behind spell and thus couldn't make your own<br /> <br /> Edit: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1017330-how-to-hide-yourself-and-why-it-s-not-possible#post1017330\">Continue in this thread</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 12-14-2016, 05:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T14:57:28-08:00","id":1017335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1016651-reign-of-the-exarchs?p=1017326#post1017326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> You do realize that there is a whole chapter about creative thaumaturgy? Rulling let's you do things that can happen and bumping into somene is one of those things. It's what Fate does, you wish something and tadaa.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;What Fate does&quot; is allow circumstances to align in a fashion that grants you conveniences as laid out by the confines of the spell's purpose and duration. Fate is not complication-free wishcasting \u2014 you get weird roundabout routes and lucky coincidences, not instant shortcuts around the long-term legwork.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And well. I hate this little paragraph in Time about using attainmant only with spells that ask for it. It's a throwback to 1ed when you didn't knew the principles behind spell and thus couldn't make your own </div> </div> </div>I really, really don't care how much you dislike not being able to run roughshod over the setting based on a failure to read the mechanics. Temporal Sympathy required you to be casting on the subject in the present even before the errata, which doesn't do you much good if they're in a Pocket Dimension you can't access.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T06:37:54-08:00","id":1017620,"title":"","content":"A few tips on my favorite adventure from that book:<br /> <br /> - The Omnium isn't sentient, but its Goetia are. If someone suggests turning them on the Scepter's defense system (maybe by convincing them if the characters die, Sutterton Farms will be destroyed anyway-the Exarchs do not love their creations), humor them. It fits with the theme of Control to have the Exarchs' own paranoia about their spells going rogue turn on them.<br /> <br /> - Figure out a way to knock off Control and/or Wish Fulfillment dots. If your players are anything like me and like to RP fundamentally wounded characters, at least one of those pseudo-Traits is going to get really high, higher than you can realistically succeed at &quot;wake up&quot; rolls with. Control's a nasty thing, so losing dots of that could be symbolic of showing negative consequences and how it ultimately harms the character, as well as Virtuous behavior that results in lessening domination (starving the inner Exarch). Wish Fulfillment, however? Lowering Wish Fulfillment probably requires <i>hurting </i>the character in some way, making the dream a nightmare. Even in-character, the Omnium probably ensues Wish Fulfillment is more stable; that's the real honey that traps its victims, because even Jesus has desires-Control requires people getting mean, all Wish Fulfillment needs is to offer a situation to help loved ones with, one that just so happens to coincide with someone's deepest desires...<br /> <br /> - Be really clear about Psychic Repercussions, and if the players honestly didn't believe you when you said that the Omnium's maker included a final curse of spite (because honestly, why should they in a chronicle which <i>you're supposed to lie to them</i>), include some plot hook of lifting the curse. Odds are players aren't going to be happy with a three-die penalty to their Aspirations simply because the Exarchs are sore losers and they were are too close to starving to death to try a humane solution.<br /> <br /> As a general note, given how (A) the Exarchs definitely exist in 2E, though maybe not in any sentient form, and (B), the new Wisdom meter, I would suggest most of the Dethroned Queen's spells <i>not </i>be inherent acts of hubris. Even besides the fact that sanity is less doubtful when the Exarchs are <i>right there </i>and it depends on an idea of &quot;celestial order&quot; that was always shaky and somewhat hypocritical in 2E (as the Seers are more or less explicitly <i>parasites </i>of that order), a truly useful Wisdom sin of a spell is going to be inured as some point, allowing increased risk of Paradox in return for knowing exactly who has their puppet strings being pulled. I <i>would, </i>however, make it so that using the spells for anything except breaking Exarchy or that collateral damage in breaking Exarchy is a sin, and with varying penalties (as you are denying the Queen's sacrifice and proving yourself just as corrupt as the Tyrants). Yes, this means it grows substantially easier to make a mistake with every more powerful piece of the Regalia. This is intentional.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T09:24:28-08:00","id":1017683,"title":"","content":"Thanks for everyone's input thus far.<br /> <br /> How is resonance handled in 2e? It was super prominent under Mage Sight in 1e. Is that still the case? There's a lot of references to it in RoE.<br /> <br /> Also, are there any cosmological inconsistencies in RoE from a 2e perspective? I mean, other than that the Exarchs are definitely real now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T09:28:35-08:00","id":1017685,"title":"","content":"If Gawain is using magic to hide and the Seers are using magic to find him. Would you not get a Clash of Wills?<br /> <br /> I assume even Fate magic requires some mechanism of the Fallen world to do it's thing. Does Fate use sympathy to get its information?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11799-rbawintrow","name":"RBAWintrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11799_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T09:55:16-08:00","id":1017690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1016651-reign-of-the-exarchs?p=1017683#post1017683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How is resonance handled in 2e? It was super prominent under Mage Sight in 1e. Is that still the case? There's a lot of references to it in RoE.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's still/more explicitly the same phenomenon as spirits gain Essence from directly, and the wider implications are more readily visible.<br /> <br /> Goetia (i.e. Astral entities) are fed by Resonance in the same manner as spirits are, and Making an Avernian Gate with magic has rather further-reaching repercussions when it gives the area around the Iris a Resonance of Death.<br /> <br /> Ley lines both conduct types of Resonance along their length and regularly intersect with powerful Hallows, which flavors the Mana in those places with qualities that makes it more useful for casting spells appropriate to that Resonance; intersections of ley lines further offer a benefit tied to a Gross Arcanum related to the Node's types of Resonance (the &quot;ancient Atlantean generator&quot; effect is tied to Forces, for instance) to mages who use an appropriate Unveiling spell from Prime or the Gross Arcanum in question.<br /> <br /> Your character's personal Signature Nimbus now serves as an innate marking mechanism that's relevant to things like Familiars and soul stones, and is readily discernible to anyone using Focused Mage Sight on the subjects of your non-Rote spells.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T09:14:33-08:00","id":1018118,"title":"","content":"I still don't get why Aidan wouldn't just cast an apportation spell to grab The Ring with his Sympathetic connection instead of bothering with the PCs at all.<br /> <br /> I suppose one solution is just to reduce his Sympathy to the artifact and say they were just following Gawain all along until he gave them the slip and then now they've traced his last whereabouts to the PCs and assume they have it now.<br /> <br /> Any other suggestions that fit with 2e mechanics?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T09:56:48-08:00","id":1018130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1016651-reign-of-the-exarchs?p=1018118#post1018118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still don't get why Aidan wouldn't just cast an apportation spell to grab The Ring with his Sympathetic connection instead of bothering with the PCs at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because even though Apportation isn't a conjunctive spell anymore, &quot;simply teleport this discrete object&quot; is still above Aidan's pay grade. The next best option is Co-Location, but that's eating all his free Reach to cast sympathetically, plus it costs Mana, risks reprisal along with detection, and likely needs either a spell control slot or extra Potency to use effectively to lower or circumvent the sympathetic Withstand.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, he's got a seven-dot Profane Urim at his disposal, which has a better casting pool for its effect than he does for his strongest points.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}